<reference id="config-fields-ipv6">
  <title>IPv6 configuration field</title>
  <shortdesc>Use the <codeph>FEATURE_LISTEN_IP_VERSION</codeph> field to configure whether Red Hat Quay listens on IPv4, IPv6, or dual-stack networks.</shortdesc>
  <refbody>
    <section>
      <p>You can use the <codeph>FEATURE_LISTEN_IP_VERSION</codeph> configuration field to specify which IP protocol family Red Hat Quay should listen on: IPv4, IPv6, or both (dual-stack). This field is critical in environments where the registry must operate on IPv6-only or dual-stack networks.</p>
      <table>
        <title>IPv6 configuration field</title>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="col_1" colwidth="50*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_2" colwidth="16.6666*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_3" colwidth="33.3334*"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Field</entry>
              <entry>Type</entry>
              <entry>Description</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>FEATURE_LISTEN_IP_VERSION</b>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>String</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>Enables IPv4, IPv6, or dual-stack protocol family. This configuration field must be properly set, otherwise Red Hat Quay fails to start.
<b>Default:</b><codeph>IPv4</codeph><b>Additional configurations:</b><codeph>IPv6</codeph>, <codeph>dual-stack</codeph></p>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <p outputclass="title">
        <b>IPv6 example YAML</b>
      </p>
      <codeblock outputclass="language-yaml"># ...
FEATURE_LISTEN_IP_VERSION: dual-stack
# ...</codeblock>
    </section>
  </refbody>
  <related-links>
